# VPS-only TLS termination (docker-compose.prod.yml adds this service -
# never part of local dev/test). One free Let's Encrypt cert for
# {$VPS_DOMAIN} (a cert is scoped to a hostname, not a port), reused
# across every port below via TLS SNI - so the existing per-service port
# scheme (every frontend's own api.ts) needs no restructuring into
# per-service subdomains. Each block just terminates TLS and reverse-proxies
# plaintext to the same container:port the host used to publish directly -
# see docker-compose.prod.yml's own comment for why those services stop
# publishing to 0.0.0.0 once this exists.
#
# Ports mirror .env's *_PORT values - if you change one there, mirror it
# here too (this file has no access to .env's variable names, only
# VPS_DOMAIN passed through docker-compose.prod.yml's environment:).
#
# If host port 80 is ever NOT free (e.g. this VPS gets a real nginx site
# again later) see docker-compose.prod.yml's own port-80 comment and this
# file's git history (2026-09-21) for the workaround: Caddy's ACME
# listener moves to host port 8078, plus one new nginx server block
# forwarding just /.well-known/acme-challenge/ to it.
#
# Classic frontends retired 2026-09-30 (docs/redesign-rollout-plan.md,
# "Retiring the classic frontends"): port 8090 (SHELL_PORT, "the default
# URL") now serves web-frontend instead of shell; the signal-engine-
# frontend/execution-frontend/manual-trading-frontend blocks that used to
# sit here (ports 8085/8081/8084) are gone along with those containers.
# market-data-frontend keeps its own block - it's operator tooling (Dhan/
# Delta feed status, instrument-master sync, Dhan token renewal), not an
# end-user screen, and has no web/frontend equivalent. Every backend port
# is untouched: web-frontend's own build reaches them at these exact same
# addresses (its VITE_*_PORT build args), same as every classic frontend
# already did.

{$VPS_DOMAIN}:8090 {
	reverse_proxy web-frontend:80
}

{$VPS_DOMAIN}:8000 {
	reverse_proxy signal-engine-backend:8000
}

{$VPS_DOMAIN}:8083 {
	reverse_proxy market-data-frontend:80
}

{$VPS_DOMAIN}:8001 {
	reverse_proxy market-data-backend:8000
}

{$VPS_DOMAIN}:8002 {
	reverse_proxy execution-backend:8000
}

{$VPS_DOMAIN}:8004 {
	reverse_proxy accounts-backend:8000
}
